    {
     "type": "tip",
     "tag": "Spanish speaker alert",
     "title": "\"¿Qué hacés?\" is not \"What do you do?\"",
     "paras": [
      "<b>What do you do?</b> asks about your job: <i>I'm a deck cadet.</i>",
      "<b>What are you doing?</b> asks about now: <i>I'm lashing the drums.</i>",
      "On deck, people almost always mean <b>now</b>."
     ],
     "avoid": "What do you do? (when you mean right now)"
    },
    {
     "type": "choice",
